# Environments and bytecode
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Checkpoints: 1.2 GB, re-downloadable (pipeline.checkpoint prints the modelscope command).
weights/

# Derived artifacts.  cache/ is ~50 MB per task set and its file names encode the fingerprint of
# the template and token budgets; runs/ holds trained heads plus their config+history.  Both are
# reproducible from the code plus the downloads above, so neither belongs in history.
cache/
runs/

# The upload-ready ModelScope package, produced by scripts/build_modelscope_pkg.py from `runs/` +
# `packaging/`.  Its authored parts (the card prose, service.py, selfcheck) live in packaging/ and
# *are* tracked; this is only the assembled copy.
dist/

# A harness that saved a torch pickle here wrote a 3 KB stray next to the JSON/TXT
# results it duplicates; results/ is evidence, and evidence is text.
experiments/results/*.pt

# The console transcript a chain writes next to its JSON, and whose `*_RC=` lines it then greps to
# decide whether a step already ran.  That is run state, not evidence: the numbers live in the
# JSONs the card and the acceptance script read, and a fresh checkout has no `runs/` either, so a
# chain on a new clone has to re-run regardless.  46 of these were 0.96 MB -- half the repo.
experiments/results/*.log

# Reference material kept beside the code but never imported: `fla/` (flash-linear-attention's
# RWKV-7 modules), `rwkv_official/` (the `rwkv` 0.8.32 package's model + tokenizer source), and
# `hf_0.4b_tensor_names.json` -- which is the HuggingFace `model.safetensors.index.json` for the
# 0.4b checkpoint (795 HF-named entries with data_offsets), kept to compare HF naming against the
# native `.pth` layout (798 tensors, `blocks.N.att.*`); the two name sets do not overlap.
# `git grep "refs/"` over the tracked source is empty, so nothing here is a runtime dependency.
# They are re-fetchable (`rwkv` 0.8.32 and flash-linear-attention from a package index), but only the
# rwkv copy records its version on disk -- the fla files carry no version marker, so treat that
# directory as a snapshot of whatever was installed when it was taken.
refs/

# Secrets.  The online teacher's DashScope key lives here and must never reach history; nothing in
# the tree reads it except by `set -a; . ./.env; set +a` in the shell that launches a teacher run.
.env
